.TH RCTL-REMOTE-DESKTOP 1 "2026-08-01" "Remote Control 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rctl-remote-desktop \- start the Remote Control desktop client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rctl-remote-desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rctl-remote-desktop
starts the graphical Remote Control client through its systemd user service.
If a systemd user manager is unavailable, it starts the client directly.
.PP
Remote access remains disabled until the local user signs in and explicitly
enables access from devices on the same account.
.SH USER SERVICE
Inspect or stop the running client with:
.PP
.nf
systemctl --user status rctl-remote-desktop.service
systemctl --user stop rctl-remote-desktop.service
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rctl-remote/services.json
Per-user service endpoint configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rctl-remote/controlled-access.json
Per-user controlled-access preference.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
